# Workflow plan step C3 (docs/WORKFLOW_PLAN.md, 2026-11-14): the CalculiX Run page by analysis type. The beam starter as it
# comes: linear static, solved in one increment. Then with NLGEOM and a first increment of 0.2: increments of Newton
# iterations. Then as a *FREQUENCY step: the list of modes, the equal pair of a square section, and the first mode against
# the cantilever's hand calculation (83.5 Hz).
# On one thread for the modes: with several, ccx's eigensolver now and then returns a spurious negative eigenvalue.
action go.new
wait-until page New case
click new-prog:calculix
wait 5
click label:Cantilever beam
wait 5
click clone-name
key A ctrl
type c3beam
click clone-go
wait-until page Overview timeout 10
click nav:run
wait-until page Run
click run-go
wait-until job finished timeout 120
wait 30
assert text What CalculiX did
assert text Solved in one increment
assert text Solver time
screenshot $OUT/c3_static.png
shell sed -i 's/^\*STEP$/*STEP, NLGEOM, INC=100/; s/^\*STATIC$/*STATIC\n0.2, 1./' beam.inp
wait 60
click run-go
wait-until job finished timeout 120
wait 30
assert text Nonlinear static in increments
assert text Step time reached 1 in increments from 0.2
screenshot $OUT/c3_nonlinear.png
shell sed -i 's/^\*STEP, NLGEOM, INC=100$/*STEP/; /^0.2, 1.$/d; s/^\*STATIC$/*FREQUENCY\n6/; /^\*CLOAD/,+1d; /^\*NODE PRINT/,+1d' beam.inp
wait 60
note one thread: with several, the eigensolver can return a spurious negative eigenvalue now and then (seen 1 run in 4)
click np-dec
click np-dec
click np-dec
click run-go
wait-until job finished timeout 120
wait 30
assert text The modes
assert text Modes 1 and 2 have the same frequency
assert text By hand, a cantilever's first bending mode: f1
screenshot $OUT/c3_modes.png
